  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe batch settlement and revenue adjustment entry points (`batchTransfers`, `rBatchTransfers`, `adjustrBalance`, and `cancelrBalanceAdjustment`) all describe “Contract must not be paused” in their requirement comments, but none of them include the `whenNotPaused` modifier. This leaves the Pausable circuit breaker unused for these privileged flows even though less-privileged mint/burn and transfer functions are correctly gated by `whenNotPaused`.\n\nImpact \n\nAfter the owner calls `pause()`, the validator can still net balances through `batchTransfers`/`rBatchTransfers`, moving user funds without restriction, and the revenue admin can continue rewriting restricted balances via `adjustrBalance`/`cancelrBalanceAdjustment`. The intended emergency stop therefore fails to halt the highest privilege operations, allowing continued asset shuffling or accounting changes during an incident response window\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nEnforce the pause circuit breaker on all privileged settlement and revenue-adjustment paths by adding the `whenNotPaused` modifier to `batchTransfers`, `rBatchTransfers`, `adjustrBalance`, and `cancelrBalanceAdjustment`. This aligns the behavior with the documented requirement and with other token flows already protected by Pausable (e.g., `mint`, `burn`, and transfers)",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity \n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {ERC20Faucet} from \"../src/ERC20Faucet.sol\";\nimport {WERC7575ShareToken} from \"../src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol\";\nimport {WERC7575Vault} from \"../src/WERC7575Vault.sol\";\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n/// @dev Demonstrates that pausing the ShareToken does not halt privileged flows\n///      such as batch netting and revenue adjustments. Even after pause(), the\n///      validator/revenue admin can continue moving balances and rewriting\n///      restricted balances.\ncontract PauseBypassPoC is Test {\n    WERC7575Vault public vault;\n    WERC7575ShareToken public shareToken;\n    ERC20Faucet public token;\n\n    address public owner;\n    address public validator;\n    uint256 public validatorPrivateKey;\n    address public user1;\n    address public user2;\n\n    uint256 constant TOTAL_SUPPLY = 10e9 * 1e18;\n    uint256 constant AMOUNT = 100 * 1e18;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        owner = address(this);\n        (validator, validatorPrivateKey) = makeAddrAndKey(\"validator\");\n        user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n        user2 = makeAddr(\"user2\");\n\n        token = new ERC20Faucet(\"USDT\", \"USDT\", TOTAL_SUPPLY);\n        shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"wUSDT\", \"WUSDT\");\n        vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(token), shareToken);\n\n        shareToken.registerVault(address(token), address(vault));\n        shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycAdmin(validator);\n        shareToken.setRevenueAdmin(validator);\n\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user1, true);\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.setKycVerified(user2, true);\n\n        // Fund users with the underlying token and mint shares to them via the vault\n        assertTrue(token.transfer(user1, AMOUNT * 10));\n        assertTrue(token.transfer(user2, AMOUNT * 10));\n\n        vm.startPrank(user1);\n        token.approve(address(vault), AMOUNT * 2);\n        vault.deposit(AMOUNT, user1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.startPrank(user2);\n        token.approve(address(vault), AMOUNT * 2);\n        vault.deposit(AMOUNT, user2);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function testBatchSettlementStillWorksWhilePaused() public {\n        shareToken.pause();\n        assertTrue(shareToken.paused(), \"pause() should put share token in paused state\");\n\n        uint256 startUser1 = shareToken.balanceOf(user1);\n        uint256 startUser2 = shareToken.balanceOf(user2);\n        uint256 moveAmount = startUser1 / 2;\n\n        address[] memory debtors = new address[](1);\n        address[] memory creditors = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n\n        debtors[0] = user1;\n        creditors[0] = user2;\n        amounts[0] = moveAmount;\n\n        // During an incident response window, the validator can still net balances\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.batchTransfers(debtors, creditors, amounts);\n\n        // Funds move despite pause(), proving the circuit breaker does not guard this path\n        assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(user1), startUser1 - moveAmount, \"user1 balance should decrease while paused\");\n        assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(user2), startUser2 + moveAmount, \"user2 balance should increase while paused\");\n    }\n\n    function testRevenueAdjustmentStillWorksWhilePaused() public {\n        shareToken.pause();\n        assertTrue(shareToken.paused(), \"pause() should put share token in paused state\");\n\n        uint256 ts = block.timestamp;\n        uint256 initialRBalance = shareToken.rBalanceOf(user1);\n\n        // Revenue admin can rewrite restricted balances while paused\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.adjustrBalance(user1, ts, 10 * 1e18, 15 * 1e18);\n        assertEq(shareToken.rBalanceOf(user1), initialRBalance + 5 * 1e18, \"rBalance should increase while paused\");\n\n        vm.prank(validator);\n        shareToken.cancelrBalanceAdjustment(user1, ts);\n        assertEq(shareToken.rBalanceOf(user1), initialRBalance, \"rBalance reset proves adjustment executable while paused\");\n    }\n}\n```",
